course: dictionary
lesson: 14255
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing. The context, meaning the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer chose. «The nestling chirped loudly for its mum.» Chirped and mum show that a nestling here is a baby bird.
explain: «The children were nestling under the warm blanket.» Here nestling is a verb. It means settling snugly and comfortably, and the words under the warm blanket are the clue. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: «A village nestling in the valley» describes a place that lies sheltered and safe, with hills around it. The writer uses nestling to paint a cosy picture. When you meet a word in a description, ask what picture it helps you see.
fact: A nestling is a noun: a baby bird that is too young to leave the nest.
fact: Nestling is also a verb form (the -ing form of nestle), meaning settling snugly or lying in a sheltered place.
fact: In science, a young bird grows in stages: hatchling, then nestling, then fledgling, when it is learning to fly.
fact: «Nestling» can paint a cosy picture: «a cottage nestling among the hills».
fact: Check the context: if the sentence is about a bird, nestling is a noun; if it is about someone or something settling or sheltered, it is a verb.
exercise: «The nestling opened its beak wide, waiting for its mum to bring a worm.» What is a nestling? | A grown-up bird that has flown far away | A bird that can swim across the lake | *A baby bird too young to leave the nest | A bird's nest made of mud and grass
exercise: «Ben was nestling under his cosy duvet.» What does nestling mean here? | Lost and frightened in the dark | Running very fast | *Settling snugly and comfortably | Shouting loudly at the window
exercise: «The farm is nestling in a quiet valley between two hills.» What does nestling suggest about the farm? | *Lying in a sheltered place | Running down the hill | Flying high above the hills | Growing very tall
test: Which stage comes after nestling, when a young bird is learning to fly? | Hatchling | Adult | Egg | *Fledgling
test: «The cottage was nestling among the hills.» What picture does this give? | *A cosy cottage tucked safely among the hills | A cottage that is moving fast | A cottage on fire | An empty cottage with no windows
exam: Which sentence uses nestling to mean a baby bird? | «The boat was nestling by the pier.» | *«The nestling chirped for its mum.» | «She was nestling her head on the pillow.» | «The cat was nestling in the sun.»
